{"uid":"2fdd467244377d64","name":"test_the_default_mode_case_ignores_an_ambient_pythonuserbase_mode_override","fullName":"tests.test_host_like_dev_layout_supplemental_run#test_the_default_mode_case_ignores_an_ambient_pythonuserbase_mode_override","historyId":"29be9b75ccad7fe5e679190d4c23b767","time":{"start":1791919562873,"stop":1791919562906,"duration":33},"description":"Regression pin for the nightly `unset`-mode dev-layout matrix cells\n    (`docker run -e HOST_LIKE_DEV_LAYOUT_PYTHONUSERBASE_MODE=unset`): that\n    env var is set for the WHOLE container, so it is already present in\n    `os.environ` when this module's own `-m fast` run executes inside it --\n    including for this exact test process. Before `_run`'s fix (popping\n    that var before applying any caller-supplied `extra_env`), a caller\n    that supplied no override of its own (like the sibling parametrized\n    test's \"exported-default-mode\" case) silently inherited that ambient\n    value instead of exercising the script's own true default, because\n    `_run` built the child's environment from `dict(os.environ)` with\n    nothing stripped. This test reproduces exactly that ambient condition\n    (`monkeypatch.setenv`, no override supplied) and asserts the nested\n    script invocation still resolves to \"exported\" mode regardless -- it\n    fails at 9b72b700 (where `_run` copied `os.environ` unstripped) and\n    passes once `_run` pops the var first.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Regression pin for the nightly <code>unset</code>-mode dev-layout matrix cells<br />\n(<code>docker run -e HOST_LIKE_DEV_LAYOUT_PYTHONUSERBASE_MODE=unset</code>): that<br />\nenv var is set for the WHOLE container, so it is already present in<br />\n<code>os.environ</code> when this module's own <code>-m fast</code> run executes inside it --<br />\nincluding for this exact test process. Before <code>_run</code>'s fix (popping<br />\nthat var before applying any caller-supplied <code>extra_env</code>), a caller<br />\nthat supplied no override of its own (like the sibling parametrized<br />\ntest's &quot;exported-default-mode&quot; case) silently inherited that ambient<br />\nvalue instead of exercising the script's own true default, because<br />\n<code>_run</code> built the child's environment from <code>dict(os.environ)</code> with<br />\nnothing stripped. This test reproduces exactly that ambient condition<br />\n(<code>monkeypatch.setenv</code>, no override supplied) and asserts the nested<br />\nscript invocation still resolves to &quot;exported&quot; mode regardless -- it<br />\nfails at 9b72b700 (where <code>_run</code> copied <code>os.environ</code> unstripped) and<br />\npasses once <code>_run</code> pops the var first.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791919562850,"stop":1791919562850,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791919562850,"stop":1791919562859,"duration":9},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791919562859,"stop":1791919562859,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_scrub_notifier_env_in_process","time":{"start":1791919562859,"stop":1791919562866,"duration":7},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_stub_wait_out_backoff_at_cl